portance value news May themselves not  be directly comparable but yet there  seems to be this sort of expectation  that some kind of high level insights of  these methods should be comparable right  so because we are all kind of combining  them in this category of feature  attribution-based methods that seems to  be expectation when they try to use  these methods in practice in fact this  is very nicely summarized by this one  quote that we had in our study one of  the participants basically articulated  this problem very clearly which was you  know the values generated by different  explanation methods are clearly  different so I would not really  characterize the disagreement based on  that but I would at least want these  methods to give me consistent insights  right so the explanations should I agree  on what are the most important features  the ordering among them and so on for me  to derive consistent insights get a  consistent answer so that I can tell to  my bosses and clients but they don't and  that's a problem for me and and we just  don't know like how to go forward right  so after doing the study we basically  took all these inputs and we started  formalizing the notion of what  constitutes disagreement between two  explanations right and essentially we  try to sort of like put notations and  mathematical formulations on uh what  they exactly described for example  feature agreement in the top K was very  important which means what fraction of  the features in the top K features  matches between two explanations  generated by two different methods rank  agreement means not only should you know  the top K features match but also the  ranking or the ordering among them  should match sign agreement is basically  looking for the fraction of the features  which not only appear commonly in the  top five of two explanations but also  their signs or the directions of their  contributions match and sign rank is  basically uh with a fraction of features  which not only appear in the top K but  their rank should match within top K the  sign or the direction of contribution  should also match right so we just  captured the different things or the  criteria that these practitioners had uh  just into uh this kind of quantifiable  formulas right and we also looked at  like a couple of other things like  Spearman rank correlation coefficient  and pairwise rank agreement and in this  case practitioners were often having use  cases where they would try to ask  questions like oh is salary more  important than credit score right uh can  you tell me like which one is more  important for the prediction so they had  some features of interest that they  cared about and they wanted again  consistent answers from different  methods with respect to questions like  these uh so we also tried to capture  that with these two metrics one is rank  correlation just a simple Spearman rank  correlation coefficient the other is  pairwise rank agreement which is  basically the fraction of the feature  features in a set of features of  Interest we care about for which the  pairwise ranking or the ordering Remains  the Same across two explanations  and after coding up all these metrics we  actually went and carried out an  empirical analysis or to check uh which  of the explanation methods actually  disagree based on these metrics uh and  we did this kind of analysis with all  the postdoc explanation methods that I  just described very briefly for real  world data sets capturing tabular text  and image data eight different model  classes including you know basic models  like logistic regression to like large  deep Nets to rnns and so on and we  actually found several disagreements  between these methods like across all  these classes of models across different  types of data sets and you know between  all these different exclamation methods  right so that was a consistent pattern  that we observed which was also sort of  agreeing with what the practiti